# newops_range_tracker_limit: A blocks-setup task's mapped-range tracker filled to its limit and past it.  One task of 15 x 4096 pages at depth 2, every leaf the same RAM page, and 30,720 one-page MapMemory2 commands at every other page (written with mem_seq, 2032 at a time into alternate halves of the largest root FIFO) fill 128 blocks of 240 runs: each run past a full last block opens a new one. Then: 1. a map into a gap of block 0 finds all 128 blocks full, compacts them,    which moves nothing, and faults "Range too complex" after the host    has mapped the page; 2. one run unmapped in block 64 leaves it 239; a map into a gap near the    end of block 127 compacts: every block from 64 on takes one run from    the next, block 127 has room, and the map completes; 3. a map into block 0 faults again (all full once more); 4. 200 runs unmapped in each of blocks 10 and 11; a map into block 0    compacts: block 10 takes all of block 11's 40 runs and removes it,    the rest cascade, and with 127 blocks the full block 0 is split and    the map completes; 5. a 1000-page map and a 1500-page unmap across several blocks. Blocks only: map and isolate map through the memory map, which has no tracker. Block calls are locked as counts and a digest: one FIFO, one task, each batch waited for, so their order is the command order.
